@startuml

!include fta_metamodel.puml

$FailureMode("Proxy cannot be created with valid handle when service is offered", "mw_com.ProxyCannotBeCreatedWithValidHandleWhenServiceIsOffered")

' - An fta should have consequences up high and causes lower.
' - The consequences should be related to the contract of the function. E.g. if Proxy::Create opens shm but this isn't part of the official contract, then failing 
'   to open shared memory should not be considered a potential issue in Proxy::Create. Instead, GetNewSamples, SetReceiveHandler etc would all have consequences 
'   that the shared memory is not yet set up. The requirement to address these issues may still be for Proxy::Create, but that way we see exactly why a certain
'   event can cause a failure i.e. creating a proxy without shared memory is potentially fine. But calling GetNewSamples without is not.
' - Always need to think "how can this event cause the failure mode".

$OrGate("OrGate1", "Communication.ProxyCannotBeCreatedWithValidHandleWhenServiceIsOffered")
